# Vulnerabilities the proxy-image scan accepts for now: exceptions E-12 and E-15 in
# docs/policies/dependencies.md. Only the Caddy image's scan reads this file; ours stays strict.
# Each line expires on its date, after which the scan fails on it again.

# golang.org/x/net v0.60.0 in caddy:2.11.9, first seen on 2026-11-18: a denial of service in the
# HTML parser (golang.org/x/net/html) on crafted HTML. Fixed in x/net 0.62.0, in no Caddy release
# yet. Only smallstep's command-line help formatting imports the parser (caddypki → smallstep
# certificates → cli-utils/usage); nothing on Caddy's HTTP request path does. Exception E-12.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-12-18

# Go's net/http (stdlib 1.27.3) in caddy:2.11.9, first seen on 2026-11-18: an HTTP/1 server can
# crash when a MaxBytesReader limit is hit while the handler writes the response headers. Fixed in
# Go 1.27.4, in no Caddy release yet. Caddy uses MaxBytesReader only for `request_body` and its admin
# API; our Caddyfile has no `request_body` any more (matchers refuse a body with no length or one
# over 28 MiB), and the admin API is local to the container (Docker) or off (native). Exception E-15.
CVE-2026-97054 exp:2026-12-18
